import SwiftUI

struct FAQView: View {
    private let entries: [(String, String)] = [
        ("Set up IKEv2", "1. Obtain a server address, certificate identity (remote ID), username and password from your provider.\n2. Create an IKEv2 profile. Enter the exact remote ID from the certificate.\n3. Save, select it on Connect, and approve iOS's VPN configuration prompt.\n4. Verify the system reports connected. This build supports EAP username/password, not client-certificate provisioning. Never disable certificate verification to work around an error."),
        ("Set up IPsec", "Choose IPsec (IKEv1), enter the server, username, password and pre-shared secret, and any provider-required group/local ID. Save and connect. Prefer IKEv2 when the gateway supports it. A bad shared secret or unsupported proposal prevents negotiation."),
        ("Set up WireGuard", "Get a peer configuration from your own server or provider, including private/public keys, endpoint, allowed IPs and DNS. This build securely stores imported .conf files but needs WireGuardKit linked and an adapter before it can connect. WireGuard uses UDP; TCP is not an interchangeable setting. See the developer engine guide."),
        ("Set up OpenVPN", "Obtain the complete .ovpn file and its required certificates/keys. Import it into a saved OpenVPN profile and choose the transport your server actually offers. This build requires an OpenVPN engine integration before connection is available; it will not pretend the imported file is active."),
        ("Set up SSTP", "SSTP typically uses TLS on TCP 443. You need an SSTP gateway, trusted certificate and credentials. A licensed/audited SSTP packet-tunnel adapter is not included, so this profile type is informational and cannot connect yet."),
        ("Why no PPTP connection?", "Modern iOS has no native PPTP VPN support. PPTP is obsolete for secure use. Migrate your gateway to IKEv2 or WireGuard rather than weakening a new app's security."),
        ("StosVPN / LocalDevVPN and JIT", "These names refer to developer tools rather than standard VPN protocols. A local virtual interface may help a separate developer workflow, but it does not grant code-signing or JIT entitlements. This app includes no JIT enabler or compatible local developer engine."),
        ("TCP versus UDP", "These are transports. UDP usually avoids head-of-line blocking and is used by WireGuard and IKEv2. OpenVPN can use either when the server supports it. SSTP uses TCP. A transport switch cannot turn one VPN protocol into another."),
        ("Set up DNS Shield", "Open DNS Shield, add hostnames or wildcard/PCRE2 rules, choose a sink IPv4 address (default 0.0.0.0), then start. Create an AdBlock DNS profile if you need to choose an upstream resolver. Allow rules win. Exact hostname rules include subdomains; *.example.com does not include example.com. Reconnect after editing rules. This development DNS engine handles unfragmented UDP queries; TCP fallback and DNSSEC behavior require further integration and device testing."),
        ("Advanced regex examples", #"Use (?=ads\.)^ads\..+$ for lookahead, ^([a-z]+)\.\1\.example$ for a backreference, or ^(?<p>a(?&p)?b)\.example$ for recursion. PCRE2 patterns are case-insensitive on normalized hostnames. Do not use JavaScript /pattern/ delimiters. Input, match, depth and heap limits stop runaway patterns; a runtime match error returns DNS failure instead of bypassing the rule."#),
        ("Domain whitelist versus DNS allowlist", "A DNS allowlist means resolve normally; it does not send that site's traffic outside an encrypted VPN. Native IKEv2 does not expose arbitrary domain-based split routing. Saved VPN bypass domains therefore block native connection until removed. Dynamic DNS, shared IP addresses, IPv6, encrypted DNS and cached connections make exact domain bypass substantially more complex than IP route exclusions."),
        ("Why use double VPN?", "Two coordinated gateways can separate entry and exit visibility and add a layer against one compromised gateway. Expect additional latency and lower throughput. It is not a substitute for trustworthy operators or browser privacy, and gateways can still collude. Choose only server-published compatible routes; two standalone iOS VPN profiles cannot simply be connected together."),
        ("Streaming, file transfers and gaming", "Streaming depends on country, throughput and the streaming service's current policies. Transfers favor low load and sustained capacity. Gaming usually favors low latency and stability. Security depends on protocol settings and gateway operations; anonymity also depends on your browser, identity and logging practices. Recommendations remain unavailable until measured data exists."),
        ("VPN permission or profile errors", "Check Settings → General → VPN & Device Management. Remove stale profiles only if you recognize them, reopen the app and approve its configuration. Confirm the app and extension are signed with the correct VPN entitlements and team. VPN transport testing requires a physical device."),
        ("Authentication or certificate failure", "Check the server's remote ID, certificate validity, device date/time, credentials and IKE proposals. Do not accept arbitrary certificates. Try another network to determine whether UDP 500/4500 is blocked. A captive portal may need to be completed before connecting."),
        ("Connected but no internet", "Disconnect to confirm basic connectivity. Check gateway forwarding/NAT, DNS, IPv6 routing, MTU and server firewall rules. Disable the local DNS shield before starting a remote VPN. A connected status alone does not prove absence of DNS/IP leaks; perform the release test checklist."),
        ("DNS ads still visible", "Already cached DNS responses, embedded first-party ads, hardcoded IP addresses, app-owned encrypted DNS and iCloud Private Relay can prevent a DNS filter from seeing a lookup. DNS rules cannot remove page elements or inspect encrypted URL paths. Test rules with a hostname and reconnect after changes."),
        ("Trials, discounts and lifetime", "The recurring plans are configured for a seven-day introductory trial subject to App Store eligibility. Lifetime is a non-consumable and requires a separate non-renewing service trial. Offer codes use Apple's redemption sheet. Referral service credit does not cancel or defer an existing subscription charge."),
        ("Family and unlimited devices", "Family products must have Family Sharing enabled in App Store Connect. Apple's group includes up to six people; the service can remove its own device cap for those members. This does not mean an unlimited number of family members. Enter invitation recipients explicitly; Apple does not disclose their email addresses to the app."),
        ("iCloud or device registration issues", "Sign in, enable iCloud for this app, and use the same Apple Account on each device. Non-family accounts have a server-enforced three-device policy once the service is configured. iCloud preference sync and VPN device authorization are separate. Credentials remain device-only. iPad is supported; a native Mac app is not included in this project."),
        ("Export diagnostic logs", "Settings → Event log lets you filter errors, warnings or all events, enable verbose operational entries, and export a text file. Review the file before sending. The developer email composer requires a configured support address and Mail account. Hide the view in Settings if you prefer.")
    ]
    var body: some View {
        List {
            ForEach(entries.indices, id: \.self) { index in
                DisclosureGroup(entries[index].0) {
                    Text(entries[index].1).font(.subheadline).textSelection(.enabled)
                        .padding(.vertical, 8)
                }
            }
        }
        .navigationTitle("Setup & FAQ")
    }
}
